# Agent Nexus — Desiderio rendering.
#
# DEPRECATED since 3.1, removed in 4.0. Depend on "webconsulting/agent-nexus"
# instead; this set only still exists so configured sites keep resolving.
#
# It used to point a higher-priority template root at a Desiderio variant of
# every plugin template. Those variants wrapped each element in
# d:layout.section + d:layout.container + d:molecule.card + a protocol badge —
# but a content element is *already* rendered inside a Desiderio section and
# container, and every plugin partial already draws its own panel and badge. The
# result was a section inside a section (py-24 on top of py-12, so 100–300px of
# empty page around every demo), a max-width inside the same max-width, a card
# inside a card, and the protocol badge printed twice.
#
# Nothing was lost by deleting them: the integration that matters is not markup
# but tokens. Resources/Public/Css/nexus-tokens.css maps every --anx-* neutral
# onto the shadcn variables Desiderio publishes (--card, --border,
# --muted-foreground …), so the widgets already follow a Desiderio site's theme,
# spacing scale and dark mode without a component wrapper.
